{
  "summary": "Nick Xenophon Team senator Skye Kakoschke-Moore announced her resignation from the Australian Senate after discovering she holds dual British citizenship through her mother. Despite previously believing she was not eligible for British citizenship based on advice received when she was 12, new guidance from the UK Home Office confirmed she inherited citizenship because her mother was born in Singapore (a former British colony) in 1957. Kakoschke-Moore, who was born in Darwin in 1985, expressed being 'heartbroken' by this discovery and plans to request the High Court determine how her vacancy will be filled. She intends to continue with NXT and hopes to return to the Senate. A recount would likely elect Tim Storrer, though Xenophon suggested the situation represents 'uncharted legal territory' following a recent High Court decision."
}
```

